+So, as run, catalog\_v4 with Muon reads pp events about as well as pp training with AdamW on held-out classes and
+with about a third more error on trained ones, but that parity is mostly the optimizer: measured against its own
+baseline, catalog\_v4 closes a sixth to a quarter of what pp training gains over catalog\_v3's windows, a third outside
+their coverage, and loses ground inside it. The AdamW arms have one seed each, all runs are short pretrainings. A clean answer needs
+the pp-trained arm with Muon at the catalog\_v4 runs' settings, two seeds; proposed to the user, not run.
